12. Engineering standards

Follow these principles throughout development:

Code quality

- Use clear function and variable names.
- Avoid unnecessary duplication.
- Separate business logic from UI logic.
- Keep modules focused.
- Handle asynchronous failures.
- Validate data at trust boundaries.
- Document complex decisions.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies.

Security

- Treat every client request as untrusted.
- Enforce authorization on the server.
- Use least-privilege database policies.
- Never expose secrets.
- Protect against replay and abuse.
- Keep sensitive operational data private.

Testing

- Test normal behavior.
- Test invalid behavior.
- Test edge cases.
- Test network failures.
- Test reconnect scenarios.
- Test authorization boundaries.
- Test compatibility with existing features.

Development discipline

- Make small changes.
- Explain why each change is necessary.
- Show which files were changed.
- Report test results honestly.
- Document known limitations.
- Never silently remove functionality.

